WEBVTT

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:10.240
He sounds different from how he usually does.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:17.860
My world is completely different from Tsukimori-kun's.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:23.260
He's in a world so distant and far away from mine.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:03.100
The Black and White Adagio

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.010
Cheers!

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:07.830
Good job in the second selection, you two!

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:09.720
You both gave great performances.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.590
Th-Thank you!

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:13.660
Thank you very much.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:16.380
We just finished the second selection tonight.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:21.450
For some reason, I am staying at Amo-san's house, whose parents are out of town.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:26.020
Even Fuyuumi-chan is here, and I was sure she'd turn down the offer.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.910
I'm... pathetic.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.000
Huh?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.620
I'm meek and not very good at competitions.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.630
I was a bag of nerves today and my notes kept drifting.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:43.140
I'm jealous that you can always play so freely, Hino-sempai.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.010
Th-That's not true!

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.470
It is, it is.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.540
You sounded great!

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:51.010
They won't announce the rankings until tomorrow,

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:52.890
but I'm sure you're going to place higher this time!

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:55.110
What? No way!

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.380
No, your performance really was lovely.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.820
You too, Fuyuumi-chan?

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.710
I didn't do it by myself.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:06.330
Umm, Hino-sempai...

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.040
Huh?

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.520
Wh-What is it?

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:16.510
Umm, would it be all right if I called you K-K-K-Kaho-sempai?

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:17.650
Huh?

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:19.130
What?!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.210
I guess I can't, huh?

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:26.100
No, it's fine.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:31.320
Thank you so much, K-K-Kaho-sempai!

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:34.360
You're so cute, Fuyuumi-chan!

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.620
Are you all right?

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.530
I'm fine.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.530
I want to be like you, Kaho-sempai.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.800
What? Stop that... I'm nothing special.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:53.630
No, you're wonderful. I want to be like you.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.770
Fuyuumi-chan...

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.720
I want to be like you, Kaho-sempai.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:17.730
I don't deserve to have someone say that about me.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.750
Kei-chan! Wake up!

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.790
I'm gonna get angry if I have to do this every day!

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.210
You're going to eat breakfast, right?

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.000
Yes, I will eat breakfast.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.250
Your hair is always so crazy in the morning.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:40.950
Oh, I got a call from Tomomi-chan.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.450
From my big sister?

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.930
Yeah, she sent you the outfits for the competition, remember?

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:49.730
She wanted to know if you liked them or not.

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:53.680
Oh, I sent her the pictures from when you were trying them on here at home.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.220
So rest assured.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:05:00.430
Good morning, Auntie.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:02.090
Yes, yes. Good morning.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:04.280
Yunoki

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.290
Azuma-san,

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.900
the main family from Kyoto is coming by tonight,

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.980
so make sure you come home early.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:16.500
Yes. I will be sure to do so, Grandmother.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.290
They announced the second selection's results!

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:25.510
1st - Ryotaro Tsuchiura
2nd - Kahoko Hino
3rd - Kazuki Hihara
4th - Azuma Yunoki
5th Keiichi Shimizu
6th - Shoko Fuyuumi
7th Len Tsukimori

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.940
Hey, hey. The two General Studies students took the top two spots.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:25.510
That's not good for the Music Department.

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:27.790
What happened to Tsukimori-kun?

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:30.240
And the first-years didn't do well at all.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:34.340
They shouldn't let them in at all. It should only be for upperclassmen.

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:38.650
Well, whatever. You probably think it's lousy too, huh, Shimizu?

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:44.040
It's a shame that I couldn't hear Tsukimori-sempai perform,

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:47.960
but Tsuchiura-sempai was amazing at the piano.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:52.560
I thought he'd be more rough,

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:57.170
but his tone was subtle and relaxed.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:03.940
There's a lot I can learn from the other participants, too.

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:06.880
2nd - Kahoko Hino

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:16.210
Placing higher than everyone...

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:20.570
Why do I feel like this now of all times?

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:22.480
Lili!

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:25.030
What's the matter? You finished in second!

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.260
What are you all depressed about?

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.540
Is it acceptable to be second because I'm in General Studies?

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:34.070
But isn't Ryotaro Tsuchiura also in General Studies?

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:35.950
Tsuchiura-kun is...

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:41.090
Wow! I can't believe you can play so well cold.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.690
What? No way.

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:46.450
I've been practicing every single day.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.880
What? Every day?

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.940
He's different.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:58.830
I knew better.

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:05.730
I decided it was unfair what I was doing and decided to do my best to make up for my audacity.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:13.070
But now... I feel so guilty.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:18.640
Oh, right! It's about time to perform maintenance on your violin again!

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.710
Huh? Oh, OK.

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:24.290
Here goes!

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.190
It should be OK now!

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:34.800
It looks like it's using up more magic than it used to,

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.260
so it'll continue to need maintenance.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:39.810
A magic violin, huh?

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:53.410
You're so kind to others, Kahoko Hino.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:57.180
I dragged you into this without permission, and yet...

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:58.830
Library

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.140
Oh, Shimizu-kun.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:08.830
The new arrival, "Melodies of Famous Songs" you requested is on the fifth shelf.

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:11.330
Thank you very much.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:18.090
Fifth... Fifth shelf...

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:23.140
I don't get it.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:26.550
Hino-sempai's performance was excellent.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:36.980
But the other student's tone's subtlety and brilliance were definitely superior,

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:40.240
so why is her performance stuck in my head?

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:43.550
Umm...

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.500
What's up, Shimizu?

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:48.680
Tsuchiura-sempai.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:49.760
Yo.

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:55.940
Congratulations on winning the second selection.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:57.730
Hey, knock it off.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:02.690
Tsuchiura-sempai is so tall.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:06.730
He's got such long arms and such big hands.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:10.390
It would be easy to carry the cello like that.

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:14.680
I want to get bigger, too.

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:15.970
Huh?

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:20.680
It's like talking to an alien.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:25.830
Well, Hino did really well, too... Jumping from last to second place.

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:29.070
That's true.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:32.300
Is something wrong?

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:36.840
No, it's just that her music is...

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:42.520
Her music? Yeah, I guess you could say it's straightforward, or without gimmicks...

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:45.200
Honest music.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:48.530
Yeah, yeah. Like that.

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:49.580
Huh?

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:53.230
Oh, you're awake.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.330
Huh? Uhh... what?

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:57.520
Shimizu wants to talk to you.

00:09:57.520 --> 00:09:58.440
Huh?

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:00.580
Hey, you have a mark on your face.

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:01.240
Huh?

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.610
You can see it on your right cheek.

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:05.320
No! Really?

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.250
Ah, how unsightly!

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:11.850
Umm, that book.

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:16.730
Huh? This book? Were you looking for it?

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:17.440
Sorry.

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:23.000
I'm really sorry.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:26.590
It's a soft sound that soothes the ears.

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:28.460
I'm going home.

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:30.130
Bye.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:39.260
So maybe I wanted to hear more of it...

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:54.670
I'm not really second place.

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:57.430
Hino?

00:10:57.430 --> 00:11:02.150
And yet, you say there's no point in performing?

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:04.130
Don't say that to me!

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:13.980
What are you doing?

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:22.000
It's odd that I got second place, when such a thing happened to you.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.280
Results are results.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:27.630
You're second. I'm last. Results are everything.

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:28.720
But...

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.990
Be proud that all the work you've put in so far got you that rank.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:35.870
But that's in the past now.

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:39.040
I will win the third selection.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:44.350
If you have time to ponder such frivolous things,

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:46.170
how about practicing some more?

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:48.590
Y-Yeah.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:15.750
Frivolous things, huh?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:18.830
Maybe he came to encourage me?

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:22.240
No, he wouldn't do that...

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:33.460
Hihara-sempai?

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.100
Oh, Hino-chan.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.640
Is something the matter?

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:44.320
Umm, actually, they sold out of all the pork cutlet sandwiches they sell at lunch.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:47.560
What? And you're depressed because of this?

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:50.940
Just kidding!

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:56.260
The truth is, my big brother's birthday is coming up.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:59.510
I can't decide on what to get him.

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:01.420
That's nice of you.

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:06.220
What was it that I got my big brother for his birthday?

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:09.070
You have a big brother, Hino-chan?

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:10.350
Yes.

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:12.440
Hihara-sempai?

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:16.430
Hey, Hino-chan, are you free today?

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:18.730
Goodbye, Yunoki-sempai.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.850
Yes, goodbye. Take care now.

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:23.070
We will!

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:28.440
Is everything all right, Azuma-sama?

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:29.320
Yes.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:30.910
Well, shall we get going?

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.070
Where are we going, Hihara-sempai?

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:36.030
How about we start by the station?

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:39.000
Oh, you two seem to be having fun.

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:40.910
Yunoki!

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:45.050
We're going to pick out a birthday present for Hihara-sempai's brother.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:47.560
Your brother?

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:52.320
She has a big brother too, so I thought she could help me pick something out.

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:56.520
Hey, Hihara, if you'd like, we can drive you there.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:59.130
What? Really? Thank you, Yunoki!

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:01.480
Can we stay with them for a bit?

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:05.120
Are you sure? You have to get home early today.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:09.950
It's fine. I'll be back before the guests leave.

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.180
What do you think of this, Hihara-sempai?

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:23.840
Hino-san, this one is cute, too.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.660
Yeah! It's really cute!

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:29.880
Hey! This is my older brother we're talking about!

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:30.960
I'm just kidding around.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:35.420
If I recall, your brother plays basketball in the gym a lot, right?

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:39.200
How about we get him something basketball-related? Like shoes.

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:41.510
Impossible. That's over my budget.

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:45.850
You have a big brother too, right, Yunoki? Have you ever given him a gift?

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:48.850
You have an older brother too, Yunoki-sempai?

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:51.770
Yes. Two older brothers, one older sister and one younger sister.

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:53.480
Wow, what a huge family.

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:57.690
But I've never given a present to my older brothers.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:15:02.710
I'd love to see them. Do they look like you?

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:06.410
Good question. Maybe not.

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:10.200
Oh, I've seen his little sister!

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.870
Her name is Miyabi-chan. She's so cute!

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:16.690
If she's Yunoki-sempai's younger sister, then I am sure she's cute.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:20.730
O-Of course, you're cute too, Hino-chan!

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:24.180
Wh-Wh-What are you saying, Hihara-sempai?

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:26.660
It's the truth! Right, Yunoki?

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:28.620
Yes. Very much so.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.080
You too, Yunoki-sempai?

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.820
Whatever!

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:37.290
Did I say something wrong?

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:39.250
Geez...

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:46.140
Those girls are staring.

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:50.100
I guess those two really stand out. Especially Yunoki-sempai.

00:15:55.250 --> 00:15:57.570
Here you go.

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:00.430
Thank you!

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:03.990
He's so polite.

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:05.520
Hey, how's this?

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.220
Hi!

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:08.810
It's nice!

00:16:08.810 --> 00:16:11.110
Yes, very much so.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:12.940
It'll look good on you too!

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:16.950
It's so big on you!

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:20.870
Geez, Hihara-sempai... Don't mess around!

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:23.240
Sorry, Hino-chan!

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:27.250
Thanks for going shopping with me.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:28.730
No, it was my pleasure.

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.470
Being with the two of them cheered me up a bit.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:35.100
What is it, Hino-chan?

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:39.160
Oh, the two of you really get along well.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:41.630
Have you known each other for a long time?

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:47.630
No, the first time we met was at the school entrance ceremony.

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:50.650
Seiso Academy Entrance Ceremony

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:55.330
I planned to leave extra early, too!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.630
Let's see... Where should I go?

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:01.310
Oh, a music student.

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:02.710
Hey, excuse me!

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:04.070
Yes?

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:06.790
He's a guy, right?

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.850
How can I help you?

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:12.620
I'm a new student. I was wondering where they assign the classes and stuff.

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:15.650
There's a sign up on the building ahead.

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:17.180
Thank you so much!

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:19.440
You're really energetic, huh?

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:24.400
Absolutely! I worked really hard to get into the Music Department here.

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:27.020
So, I'm really happy!

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:28.450
You're that happy?

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:29.600
Yes!

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:30.850
Wow.

00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:35.550
All students participating in the school entrance ceremony, please assemble in the auditorium.

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:37.440
Looks like we should hustle.

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:41.670
Yeah! Thank you, sempai!

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:43.450
Sempai?

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:47.870
Uh, to all new students, welcome to Seiso Academy.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:52.910
That guy was really calm before. Maybe he's a third-year?

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:55.140
I'll be like that when I get to my third year.

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:58.170
Hihara-sempai, teach us!

00:17:58.170 --> 00:17:59.680
Sure, see here...

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:02.500
You're so calm and collected, Hihara-sempai.

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:05.670
I'll give it my all!

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:09.380
Continuing on, we'll call on the representative of the first year class, Azuma Yunoki-kun.

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:10.390
Yes.

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:16.010
If he's the class representative, then that means he scored number one on the entrance exam.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:18.160
I wonder what he's like.

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:22.330
Looks like you made it on time.

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:26.450
And that's how Yunoki and I met.

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:29.370
That sounds just like you, Hihara-sempai.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:31.480
It's been two years since then.

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:36.180
It's tough being third-years with college exams and the competition.

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:39.530
Are you giving equal study time to both, Hihara?

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:40.630
About that...

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:43.890
Are you two going to music college?

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:49.320
Yeah, I'm going into musical theory. How about you, Yunoki?

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:54.200
I'm actually going to study economics or business. Music is only till I graduate.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:59.320
Really? I thought you'd go on to a career in music.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:05.390
Umm, thank you for driving me home.

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:06.790
You're welcome.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:11.030
By the way, congratulations on placing second in the second selection.

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:13.040
You gave a great performance.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:15.540
Th-Thank you.

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:17.930
It's hard enough for someone in the Music Department like me,

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:21.640
so it's got to be even harder for a General Studies student.

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:23.980
I've been giving it some thought.

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:26.490
Wondering if there's any point to working so hard for the competition

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:30.060
while I'm at a crucial point in my studies, as a third-year.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:33.300
So you shouldn't overdo it either, Hino-san.

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:35.100
Yunoki-sempai...

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:51.850
I thought the students from the Music Department would have it easier in the competition,

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:54.820
but it's really a lot of work for everyone.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:20:00.820
If I have time to feel guilty, then that means I should be practicing more.

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:04.430
I have to give it everything I've got!

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:11.650
This song...

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:16.070
Yunoki-sempai?

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:25.400
It's a beautiful song, but...

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:33.040
What is it? It's deep and dark...

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:38.990
You startled me, Hino-san.

00:20:38.990 --> 00:20:40.040
What's up?

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:43.270
I-I'm sorry, Yunoki-sempai!

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:45.650
Umm, that song you were playing...

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:48.020
Do you mean Albinoni's Adagio?

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:49.800
It has a pretty melody, doesn't it?

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:55.270
Y-Yes, but it sounds so sad, doesn't it?

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:57.750
Certainly.

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:01.760
But, for whatever reason, it calms me down when I play it.

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:05.410
Were you coming up here to practice too?

00:21:05.960 --> 00:21:08.880
Yes. But I'll look for another place.

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:10.860
Sorry to disturb you!

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:12.250
Excuse me!

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:13.410
Yeah?

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:20.910
Umm, Yunoki-sempai. I'm going to try to give it my all.

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:25.410
I'm sure it'll only get more difficult for me,

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:29.850
but you've got way more to worry about than me, don't you?

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:32.190
I was worried for a bit,

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:34.570
but thanks to you, I feel better now!

00:21:34.570 --> 00:21:37.610
Thank you for worrying about me.

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:40.430
Worry?

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:44.450
Me... about <i>you</i>?

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:46.250
Huh?

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:56.120
You didn't know, did you?

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:59.870
You're annoying.

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:40.100
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:36.620 --> 00:23:39.770
Lili's One Point Classic

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:46.300
The flute is an instrument that makes the sound resonate as you blow into it!

00:23:46.300 --> 00:23:49.570
It's the same principle as blowing onto the opening of a bottle to make sound come out of it.

00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:53.910
Though it's made of metal today, since it used to be made of wood,

00:23:53.910 --> 00:23:56.460
it's classified as a woodwind instrument.

00:23:56.460 --> 00:23:58.370
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:05.110
What instrument in the flute family is half the length of the flute and plays an octave higher?

00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:10.010
Next Episode

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:09.240
Umm, Yunoki-sempai, I didn't get that.

00:24:09.240 --> 00:24:10.350
What did you say?

00:24:10.350 --> 00:24:12.250
You're annoying.

00:24:12.250 --> 00:24:14.510
Gah! I'm annoying?

00:24:15.050 --> 00:24:17.760
Next episode: The Pianissimo of Guilt.

00:24:17.760 --> 00:24:20.110
I remember you...

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:22.010
The answer is...

00:24:22.820 --> 00:24:25.100
The Piccolo!
